 "limitations": [
  "Validation data was used for both early stopping and threshold selection, so validation metrics are optimistic and the threshold is fitted to a few patients.",
  "Only 81 patients from a single institution (BreakHis); no external validation.",
  "Single magnification (100X), H&E staining; other magnifications, stains or scanners are out of scope.",
  "Image-level predictions; no slide- or patient-level aggregation.",
  "Grad-CAM is computed on a coarse 7x7 grid and highlights influential regions, not diagnostic features.",
  "Research and education demo only; not for clinical use.",
  "The decision threshold (0.34) was chosen on a validation set with only 3 benign patients. Thresholds chosen the same way in the 5 cross-validation folds ranged from 0.07 to 0.98, so the exact cut-off is uncertain.",
  "In cross-validation, a fixed 0.5 threshold did at least as well on average as the validation-selected thresholds (balanced accuracy 0.886 vs 0.858).",
  "Grad-CAM sometimes highlights structures that are not diagnostic, such as adipose (fat) tissue. A highlighted region is where the model looked, not necessarily where a lesion is.",
  "The model was trained on 224x224 patches. Larger or non-square images (for example the original 700x460 BreakHis images) are squashed to 224x224, which changes tissue geometry."
